Z||000000||mshill||04-02-2000||09:43 PM||||I put a Blue Racer +1 cam into my fresh 2.8L V6 rebuild.  It has the same specs as the GM performance cam adn similar specs to the Crane Compucam that the Fiero Store sells.<P>I believe the specs are 260/270, 194/204, .398/.420.<P>I used to get about 17 mpg city and 22 mpg highway but now it seems I am getting signigicantly less 30% mileage with the cam.  Is this expected?<P>BTW, it the car really pulls hard and just sounds so much sweeter.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Raydar||04-03-2000||12:57 AM||||As it breaks in, and all the moving parts get used to all the others, your mileage will improve noticeably. You said it pulls hard... That hard pullin' uses gas, too. (But don't it feel good?)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000002||mshill||04-05-2000||03:59 PM||||Well, I filled up yesterday and I figured I am getting 15-16 mpg all city driving.  The engine now has 150+ miles on it since the rebuild.  How long before everything starts "getting used to each other" and the gas mileage increases?<BR>||||reg||1
